{#
  Renders from content/sat/* (docs/CONTENT_MODEL.md) instead of the legacy
  {% include "tracks/sat.html" %} — seventeenth track cut over, following the established pattern
  (docs/DECISIONS/0005 through 0017). index.html (deleted, WP10 step 4 — docs/DECISIONS/0023;
  still recoverable via git history) and src/_includes/tracks/sat.html (also deleted, same step)
  used to be kept as an inert rollback path — no longer needed once every track had been
  migrated and verified live.

  Notes (WP29): sat-about's real markup has a NEW block kind not seen on any prior track — a
  <div class="syllabus-map"> exam-blueprint bar chart (h3 title, one .sm-row per topic with a
  topic label, a %-width bar, a displayed percent, and a small tag span) — added as
  course_schema.json's syllabusMapBlock, rendered via partials/blocks/syllabus-map.njk. Confirmed
  reused by igcse (docs/DECISIONS/0018), with real per-row differences there (multiple tags per
  row, no inline style on the tag spans) — do not assume igcse's copy is identical.

  chapterTag's real .sat-domain-tag class reuses the existing 'category' variant but with two real
  deviations: no weight-badge span at all (weightBadge omitted, now optional in the schema), and
  an optional plain "Domain: " prefix between the emoji and the bold category name (categoryPrefix,
  new field) — sat-desmos's real tag has NO such prefix ("📌 <strong>All domains</strong>..."),
  confirming it's genuinely per-chapter, not per-track.

  Two real LaTeX-corruption bugs were found and fixed during transcription (not reproduced):
  (1) a systematic \neq → newline+"eq" corruption at 4 sites (ex. 4.D, the ch4 formula-cards
  "Domain restriction" card, the ch4 problem's solution, and the ch10 Q2 problem's solution) —
  the literal source bytes have a real newline where "\n" of "\neq" belongs, silently swallowing
  the "n"; (2) missing "\\" row-separators inside two \begin{cases}...\end{cases} piecewise
  functions (ex. 8.B and the ch8 problem) — same bug category as alg2's matrix fix (PR #117).

  The "example" callout style (course_schema.json, existing since WP22/algebra) covers sat's
  real <div class="example"><span class="xt">Worked example N.X</span>...</div> markup exactly —
  no new block kind needed for the 20 worked examples across this track's 11 chapters.

  Chapters 2/4/5 have real explorers (satLineCanvas/satExpCanvas/satFitCanvas), each with a real
  data panel and a callout.note wrapping its live-equation hint — no equationDisplay in this track
  (unlike algebra, WP28); the existing explorer.njk block.note branch already matches exactly.

  testGenerator has a real "Full official exam paper" section (hasFullExam left at its true
  default) — a 2-module Digital SAT exam generator, distinct from geo/alg2/algebra's
  hasFullExam:false tracks.
#}
